# Ghostly Dancers: "return an enchantment card from your graveyard to your hand or unlock a locked door of a Room you control".
# Neither option reaches past its owner's words. Bot1's Thought Scour mills Bot2's Oblivion Ring on turn 1, and Bot2 casts Grand
# Entryway on turn 2, its Elegant Rotunda door still locked: an enchantment card in an opponent's graveyard and a Room with a locked
# door an opponent controls. Bot1's own Grand Entryway // Elegant Rotunda is fully unlocked on turn 3, a Room you control with no
# locked door, and a second Thought Scour mills Bot1's Banishing Light. On turn 5 Ghostly Dancers enters: the only option that can
# be done (CR 608.2d) is returning Banishing Light, so it is done without asking which option (`! Bot1.Modes`): a fully unlocked
# Room of yours and a Room of an opponent's are not "a locked door of a Room you control". Oblivion Ring stays in Bot2's graveyard
# and Bot2's Elegant Rotunda stays locked. (ghostly-dancers-does-nothing-with-only-an-opponents-enchantment-card-and-locked-room
# shows the opponent's enchantment card is no option either.)

